<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom buys back more shares offmarket.</title>
<headline>Telecom buys back more shares offmarket.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom Corp of New Zealand said it bought back a further 1.3 million shares on Tuesday at $6.53/share from its major shareholders Bell Atlantic and Ameritech as part of its continuing $1 billion buyback programme.</p>
<p>The stock was three cents higher at $6.58 on market in late morning.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
